Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Scratch Build Executor P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 82446f5f-0902-48a9-8d30-7ee2247b62c3
@ [canonical_uuid] 935e020f-8c6f-49e4-b355-63eabd3b778b

& [WhyNow]
  + EVO-X2 already produces and verifies the exact inert seven-operation plan so the next smallest product-learning step is one separately authorized physical scratch build

& [WhyCommission]
  + plan semantics describe desired work but cannot safely authorize transfer extraction observation writes or process execution
  + a content-bound one-run commission makes the new authority explicit reviewable and revocable on mismatch

& [WhyRetainScratchState]
  + automatic cleanup would add destructive authority and can erase the evidence needed to diagnose a stopped offline build
  + immutable retained roots provide a bounded forensic boundary until a separately governed cleanup

& [WhyStrictOffline]
  + observing actual cached capability distinguishes reproducible local readiness from an implicit install or network-assisted success

& [Decision]
  + authorize formation and after its bookend provider-free host-free local implementation only; remote effects await implementation publication and exact commission
